[" Due to the complexity of your request, I'll provide you with a high-level outline and key components for your solution. This will include the SQL Stored Procedure code, supporting table schema, indexes, and additional scripts for setup and configuration.

**Stored Procedure: GetProductDetailsExtended**

```sql
CREATE PROCEDURE GetProductDetailsExtended
    @SupplierIDs varchar(MAX),
    @Tags varchar(MAX),
    @AdditionalParams nvarchar(MAX) = NULL,
    @@LogError int OUTPUT
AS
BEGIN
    SET NOCOUNT ON;

    DECLARE @SQLQuery NVARCHAR(MAX);
    SET @SQLQuery = 'SELECT p.*, c.CategoryName, s.SupplierName, s.ContactName, s.Phone, s.Website';
    IF(@AdditionalParams IS NOT NULL)
        SET @SQLQuery += ', ' + @AdditionalParams;

    SET @SQLQuery += ' FROM Products p';
    SET @SQLQuery += ' INNER JOIN Categories c ON p.CategoryID = c.CategoryID';
    SET @SQLQuery += ' INNER JOIN Suppliers s ON p.SupplierID = s.SupplierID';
    SET @SQLQuery += ' WHERE 1=1';

    IF(@SupplierIDs IS NOT NULL)
        SET @SQLQuery += ' AND p.SupplierID IN (' + @SupplierIDs + ')';

    IF(@Tags IS NOT NULL)
        SET @SQLQuery += ' AND p.ProductTag IN (' + @Tags + ')';

    EXEC sp_Executesql @SQLQuery, N'@LogError int OUTPUT', @LogError OUTPUT;

    IF (@LogError > 0)
    BEGIN
        INSERT INTO ErrorLog (ErrorMessage, AdditionalInfo)
        SELECT ERROR_MESSAGE(), @AdditionalParams;
    END;
END;
```

