[' Here's a high-level design for the `DynamicNetworkHealthMonitor` class in Java, adhering to your requirements. Please note that this is a skeleton structure, as actual implementation would require extensive development, testing, and refinement.

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.time.*;
import java.security.*;
import org.slf4j.*;
import akka.actor.ActorSystem;
import com.google.common.collect.*;
import io.prometheus.client.*;
import ai.h2o.*;

public class DynamicNetworkHealthMonitor {
    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(DynamicNetworkHealthMonitor.class);
    private static final ActorSystem actorSystem = ActorSystem.create();
    private final Map<String, HealthChecker> serviceCheckers;
    private final ServiceConfigService configService;
    private final AlertingService alertingService;
    private final PerformancePredictor performancePredictor;
    private final H2OAutoML h2oModel;
    private final Gauges gauges = Metrics.defaultGaugeSet();

    public DynamicNetworkHealthMonitor(ServiceConfigService configService, AlertingService alertingService) {
        this.configService = configService;
        this.alertingService = alertingService;
        this.performancePredictor = new PerformancePredictor();
        this.h2oModel = new H2OAutoML(actorSystem);
        this.serviceCheckers = ImmutableSortedMap.of();
    }

    public void start() {
        // Start monitoring services based on initial configuration
        for (ServiceConfig config : configService.getAllServices()) {
            addService(config);
        }

        // Run the main loop for continuous monitoring and dynamic reconfiguration
        Timer timer = new Timer();
        timer.schedule(new TimerTask() {
            @Override
            public void run() {
                for (HealthChecker checker : serviceCheckers.values()) {
                    boolean isHealthy = checker.checkServiceHealth();
                    if (!isHealthy) {
                        String serviceId = checker.getServiceId();
                        alertingService.sendAlert(serviceId);
                    }
                }
            }
        }, 0, Long.MAX_VALUE);
    }

    public void addService(ServiceConfig config) {
        HealthChecker newChecker = createHealthChecker(config);
        synchronized (serviceCheckers) {
            serviceCheckers.put(config.getId(), newChecker);
            logger.info("Added service {} to monitoring", config.getId());
        }
    }

    public void removeService(String serviceId) {
        synchronized (serviceCheckers) {
            serviceCheckers.remove(serviceId);
            logger.info("Removed service {} from monitoring", serviceId);
        }
    }

    // Other methods for modifying monitored services, implementing adaptive strategies, handling errors, etc.
}
```

This code includes a basic class structure for the `DynamicNetworkHealthMonitor`, with initial implementations for starting the monitor and adding/removing services. The actual implementation of each method is left as an exercise for the reader to complete, based on real-world constraints and engineering focus areas specified in your requirements.']

