// Interface for Key Management Systems (KMS)
class IKeyManager {
public:
    virtual std::string getKey(const std::string& kmsUrl, const std::string& keyId) = 0;
};

// Concrete KMS implementation using RESTful API
class RestKM : public IKeyManager {
public:
    std::string getKey(const std::string& kmsUrl, const std::string& keyId) override {
        // Implement KMS communication logic here
    }
};

// Hash computations using OpenSSL
unsigned char* sha256(const unsigned char* data, size_t length) {
    unsigned char digest[SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH];
    SHA256_CTX ctx;
    SHA256_Init(&ctx);
    SHA256_Update(&ctx, data, length);
    SHA256_Final(digest, &ctx);
    return digest;
}

// Secure key retrieval function
std::vector<unsigned char> computeHashWithKeyRetrieval(const std::string& input, const IKeyManager& kms, size_t bufferSize) {
    std::vector<unsigned char> key;
    try {
        key = kms.getKey("http://example-kms.com", "example-key"); // Replace with actual KMS URL and key ID
    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
        std::cerr << "Error retrieving key: " << e.what() << std::endl;
        return {};
    }

    unsigned char* data = new unsigned char[bufferSize];
    memcpy(data, input.c_str(), input.length());

    auto hash = sha256(data, input.length());
    delete[] data;

    std::vector<unsigned char> result(hash, hash + SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH);
    return result;
}
```

This code provides a basic implementation of a key retrieval function that computes the SHA-256 hash of an input string using a cryptographic key securely obtained from an external Key Management System (KMS). The KMS interface is defined in `IKeyManager`, and a concrete implementation using a RESTful API is provided in `RestKM`.

To integrate with different KMSs, simply create other implementations of the `IKeyManager` interface. The actual communication logic with the KMS should be implemented in the derived classes. The given example uses an HTTP-based KMS, but you can adapt it to suit other KMS types as needed.

The provided code does not include multi-threading, configuration management, or error handling thresholds. You'll need to extend this implementation for those features according to your project requirements and constraints.']

