[" Here is a high-level structure for the `DynamicEventProcessor` in Java. Note that this is not an exhaustive implementation but rather a guide for creating the required components:

```java
public class DynamicEventProcessor {
    private JsonParser jsonParser;
    private EventFilter eventFilter;
    private MessageBroker messageBroker;
    private MonitoringService monitoringService;
    private StateManager stateManager;
    private ErrorHandler errorHandler;

    public DynamicEventProcessor(JsonParser jsonParser, EventFilter eventFilter, MessageBroker messageBroker,
                                  MonitoringService monitoringService, StateManager stateManager, ErrorHandler errorHandler) {
        this.jsonParser = jsonParser;
        this.eventFilter = eventFilter;
        this.messageBroker = messageBroker;
        this.monitoringService = monitoringService;
        this.stateManager = stateManager;
        this.errorHandler = errorHandler;
    }

    public void processEvent(String jsonPayload) {
        try {
            Event event = jsonParser.parseEvent(jsonPayload);
            if (eventFilter.shouldProcess(event)) {
                processFilteredEvent(event);
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            errorHandler.handleDeserializationError(e);
        }
    }

    private void processFilteredEvent(Event event) {
        // Perform stateful operations, aggregation, transformation, etc., and update the state manager accordingly.
        stateManager.updateState(event);
        // Trigger alerts or monitoring if necessary based on event characteristics.
        monitoringService.monitorEvent(event);
    }
}
```

