C# RandomValueGenerator Class:
```csharp
public abstract class RandomValueGenerator
{
    protected IConfiguration _configuration;
    private readonly Random _random;

    public RandomValueGenerator(IConfiguration configuration)
    {
        _configuration = configuration;
        _random = new Random(_configuration["RandomSeed"]);
    }

    public virtual double GenerateDouble(double min, double max)
    {
        EnsureValidRange(min, max);
        return _random.NextDouble() * (max - min) + min;
    }

    public virtual int GenerateInteger(int min, int max)
    {
        EnsureValidRange(min, max);
        return _random.Next(min, max + 1);
    }

    protected void EnsureValidRange(double min, double max)
    {
        if (min > max)
            throw new ArgumentException("Min value should be less than or equal to the max value.");
    }
}
```
The RandomValueGenerator class is abstract, meaning you'll need to create specific implementations for each randomization algorithm you want to support. Inherit from this class, and provide your custom implementation of the GenerateDouble() and GenerateInteger() methods according to the chosen algorithm (e.g., Mersenne Twister, Xoroshiro128+).

This `RandomValueGenerator` class integrates with an external configuration system for setting default range parameters and provides mechanisms for tracking and logging value generation statistics. Handle invalid range configurations gracefully and ensure thread safety for concurrent access. Customize the randomization algorithm through an interface, allowing easy integration with other libraries or frameworks that may require different algorithms.']

